menu "LarkBridge S31 gateway"

config LARKBRIDGE_S31_ERASE_BONDS_ON_BOOT
    bool "Erase S31 settings and Bluetooth bonds on every boot"
    default n
    help
        Recovery-image option. Enable, flash and boot once to forget the bound
        Pixel, then disable and flash the normal image. Do not leave enabled.

config LARKBRIDGE_S31_ROUTE_DRAIN_GUARD_MS
    int "Silence guard before opening a new audio route (ms)"
    range 100 2000
    default 350
    help
        After the output board acknowledges and flushes a SILENCE route, keep
        both endpoints silent for this additional pipeline-drain interval.
        The default is deliberately conservative and must be tuned with the
        arrival-day stale-media boundary test.

config LARKBRIDGE_S31_EXPERIMENTAL_AEC_UPLINK
    bool "Enable unqualified ESP-SR AEC call uplink"
    default n
    help
        Keep disabled in normal images. Enabling permits processed LARK audio
        to reach the Pixel only after the route fence is open and fresh mic
        plus downlink-reference frames have passed ESP-SR AEC. This remains
        an arrival-day bench option until the documented echo-suppression,
        clipping, latency, and stability gates pass on the assembled device.

config LARKBRIDGE_S31_AEC_REFERENCE_DELAY_MS
    int "Initial acoustic-reference delay compensation (ms)"
    range 0 200
    default 160
    help
        Delays the microphone stream relative to the HFP downlink reference
        before AEC processing, compensating for I2S, downstream A2DP, car, and
        acoustic latency. The value is intentionally arrival-day tunable and
        must be measured with the assembled car/output path. The 200-ms limit
        preserves headroom in the fixed raw-microphone ring.

endmenu
